<?jelly escape-by-default='true'?>
<j:jelly xmlns:j="jelly:core" xmlns:f="lib/form" xmlns:c="lib/credentials">
<p>Choose the application files, then decide whether to keep the inventory locally, check CVEs or synchronize a deployed source. Use the help icons for examples.</p>
<f:entry title="Validate configuration only (no scan or upload)" field="preflightOnly"><f:checkbox/></f:entry>
<f:entry title="Detailed logging (safe operational details)" field="detailedLogging"><f:checkbox/></f:entry>
<f:entry title="What to scan" field="collector"><f:select/></f:entry>
<f:entry title="Action" field="mode"><f:select/></f:entry>
<f:entry title="Path relative to workspace" field="path"><f:textbox default="."/></f:entry>
<f:entry title="Application label" field="applicationLabel"><f:textbox default="application"/></f:entry>
<f:entry title="Monitor credential JSON (Secret file)" field="credentialsId"><c:select/></f:entry>
<f:entry title="Version-confirmed CVE severity threshold" field="severityThreshold"><f:select/></f:entry>
<f:entry title="Apply build policy when inventory or assessment is incomplete" field="failOnIncomplete"><f:checkbox default="true"/></f:entry>
<f:entry title="Build result when a policy is triggered" field="policyResult"><f:select/></f:entry>
<f:entry title="Include all installed Linux packages" field="allPackages"><f:checkbox/></f:entry>
<p>Build the application and install its dependencies before this step. Syft inspects existing files only. Linux means the selected Jenkins agent, not the application container or production server. API actions require administrator-approved jobs, agents and destinations.</p>
</j:jelly>
